s like grit  perseverance growth mindset  all these kind of things we associate  with social emotional learning that's  the third year the third area is just  compliance  the compliance is did you do what i told  you had to do  now again  we don't know at this time among those  what's most important for students we're  just starting to study that now a new  center has been established at the  university of chicago to look into this  harvard university has established the  center to look into social motion  learning skills we do know this you you  can't do it all  and so the means of faculty again has to  sit down and decide their priorities and  among those things what they consider  most important  then you have to develop meaningful  rubrics for it  you have to be able to communicate that  rubric to all the stakeholders parents  and students in particular  and then  make sure that you include that on your  report card in a meaningful way and in  your purpose statement that you're going  to report those things separately  that that absolutely makes sense  in terms of thinking about all of the  pieces that need to fall into place um  we are already almost that time i want  to  do  come make the circle back to mastery  learning i know you've also  have a book uh implementing mastery  learning and uh what that looks like how  do these grading practices and mastery  learning all come together to  you know make that that implementation  of mastery learning happen through these  grading practices  well it's certainly true this new  version of our book on implementing  mastery learning  is  actually a third edition it was my very  first book and benjamin bloom actually  wrote the  uh an issue forward to the book and so  we're taking those those ideas and  adapting them now to a  you know a 21st century format and one  of the things we talk about in the book  is the use of technology within mastery  learning especially as a sort of  instructional advice when you have a  so